    "display_title": "feat(store): hp and attack cooldown in the unit store (spec 35 step 5b)",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "feature/hp-and-cooldown-in-store",
    "head_commit_message": "perf(formation): the step-up works on a count grid and rechecks only changed columns\n\nSquadCompact.compact was about 95% of bury. It now reads ranks and files as\ntyped copies, keeps who holds each place as a count on a packed grid\n(SquadCompact.Held) instead of a dictionary of unit lists, filters the living\nonce, and after its first pass looks again only at units with a place in one\nof their columns changed since they were last looked at. A unit's row ahead\nlies in its own columns, so every other unit would find it held as before:\nthe same units step up in the same order, on both engines.\n\nThe spec records the copy count from tick_phases: about 1.7 million slots a\ntick at 4,096 a side, roughly 1 ms of a 219 ms tick, too little for the\nbatched-table fixes to be worth building.\n\nWaived-by: Decision 142\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KKUhViTbS7kfMBSZozDAco",
    "head_sha": "af9adefd885a4d4963a428aca68a136d9cc5c76c",
